{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/780532-first-change-and-lunar-eclipse","id":780532,"title":"First Change and Lunar Eclipse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-05T06:32:30-08:00","id":780532,"title":"First Change and Lunar Eclipse","content":"Is there anything that contradicts the idea that a werewolf who undergoes the first change during a lunar eclipse could have an auspice other than Rahu?(A lunar eclipse only happens during the full moon) I'm the ST so I can handwave it, but I'm curious. Are there any other effects on werewolves during a lunar eclipse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T06:39:25-08:00","id":780535,"title":"","content":"In the book Signs of the Moon there's a few other auspices offered. The one that occurs during a Lunar Eclipse is called Suharrahu, and are considered 'Trickster Warriors.' 'Rahu of this peculiarity embody tactical advantage as a particular Aspect of their birthright. The Suharrahu should strike first, strike in the most advantageous spot, and guarantee minimal casualties on her side in all cases.'<br /> <br /> Sounds like it's more of a subsect of rahu than its own entire Auspice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T07:37:29-08:00","id":780548,"title":"","content":"Signs of the Moon had a few additional Auspices - lunar eclipse, solar eclipse, blood moon, and &quot;stellar eclipse&quot; which I don't think is a real thing. Most of them were just slight variations on an existing Auspice, only swapping out the Auspice ability and sometimes an Auspice Skill or Affinity Gift or two. The stellar eclipse one was the only one with its own Moon Gift.<br /> <br /> The book was also pretty clear that these extra Auspices go against the setting's default assumptions, basically saying there are five Auspices for a reason, but if you want to homebrew more anyway, here are a few examples. So to answer solidork's question, a werewolf who First Changes under a lunar eclipse would be a Rahu by the default setting, but if you like the idea of them having a different Auspice, check out Signs of the Moon, it has good advice on custom Auspices and an example Lunar Eclipse Auspice. It's First Edition, but a lot of it is still applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T09:06:01-08:00","id":780579,"title":"","content":"Thanks a bunch, I'll check that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}